        "thumbnailUrl": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/VYOjWnS4cMY/maxresdefault.jpg",
        "runtimeSeconds": 245,
        "genre": "Hip-Hop"
      },
      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "shortSummary": "A mobile camera follows Childish Gambino through a warehouse as performance, celebration, gun violence, and disorder compete across foreground and background.",
          "whyItMatters": "The video uses the mechanics of spectacle to examine distraction, violence, race, and entertainment in the United States, making the viewer's shifting attention part of the work.",
          "historicalContext": "Directed by Hiro Murai and released in 2018, the video became an immediate subject of public interpretation and received the 2019 GRAMMY for Best Music Video.",
          "keyInnovation": "Long moving passages coordinate foreground choreography with incidents placed deep in the frame, forcing the viewer to choose between the central performance and the surrounding evidence."
        },
        "ja": {
          "shortSummary": "移動するカメラが倉庫内のChildish Gambinoを追い、演技、祝祭、銃による暴力、混乱が前景と背景で注意を奪い合う作品。",
          "whyItMatters": "スペクタクルの仕組みそのものを使って、米国における気晴らし、暴力、人種、娯楽を考察し、観客の移ろう注意を作品の一部にしました。",
          "historicalContext": "Hiro Muraiが監督し2018年に公開。直ちに広範な解釈の対象となり、2019年GRAMMY Best Music Videoを受賞しました。",
          "keyInnovation": "長い移動撮影の中で、前景の振付と画面奥の事件を同時進行させ、中心の演技と周囲の証拠のどちらを見るかを観客に選ばせます。"
        }
      },
